sm: OpenAI-compatible providers like Kimi emit malformed tool call names (functions:read, functions:exec) instead of canonical names (read, exec). Issue [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) – Independent confirmation of the same regression. Our issue is listed as a high-severity open regression alongside [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) and [#42270](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270), confirming that the tool dispatch failure is one of the most actively tracked blockers in the community right now. PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (tool-name normalization for Kimi's functions:exec format) was closed without merge due to reviewer concerns about the fuzzy endsWith inference logic. this looks related to [#41462](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41462) — the symptom is identical: all tools returning \\\"Tool not found\\\" immediately after upgrading from 2026.3.1 to 2026.3.2, with 2026.3.1 working fine.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8f20dd57b2a374a6\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.8638634\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35a064695eb44e23\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw v2026.1.30 Skill Loading Regression #8290\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35a064695eb44e23\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/8290\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b6980bc0ffe2a0b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: OpenClaw v2026.1.30 Skill Loading Regression #8290. [[Bug]: OpenClaw v2026.1.30 Skill Loading Regression](#top)#8290. Description: Despite a valid openclaw.json and agent.json, core skills (specifically exec and web-search) fail to load. The Gateway initializes the Telegram provider but results in an agent with 0 tools. Skills Status: 7 Eligible | 44 Missing requirements. Plugins: 2 Loaded (Telegram/Gateway) | 28 Disabled. Gateway Status: Exited with reason 1 (likely due to zero active skills). openclaw skills register and agents update return unknown option '--id' or --add-skill. openclaw skills [verb] [skill] returns: error: too many arguments for 'skills'. Manually created agent.json with capabilities and skills arrays. Requested Fix: Clarification on the \\\"44 missing requirements\\\" blocking the exec skill on Debian and restoration of CLI verbs for manual skill binding. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b6980bc0ffe2a0b\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.8568246\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6471d69f8e7836d9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026. ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6471d69f8e7836d9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24395\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6506673f6484f5f1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSummary Summary All channel plugins remain disabled despite correct configuration. Works fine in v2026.2.19, broken in v2026.2.22.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6506673f6484f5f1\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.8282873\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da53457365e12f8a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: File write/read tools intermittently produce empty files\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da53457365e12f8a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/44372\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"709a85ea2a0805b8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Bug]: File write/read tools intermittently produce empty files - regression in v2026.3.11 #44372. [[Bug]: File write/read tools intermittently produce empty files - regression in v2026.3.11](#top)#44372. The `write` and `read` file tools exhibit intermittent failures where `write` reports success but creates a 0-byte file, and `read` returns empty content for files that should contain data. The issue is observed specifically when using the `kimi-coding/k2p5` (Kimi Code) model. 1. Use OpenClaw with model `kimi-coding/k2p5` on version 2026.3.11. 2. Execute a `write` tool call to create a new file with content, e.g.:. * `read` tool should return actual file content when the file exists and contains data. * `write` reports success but file is created with 0 bytes. * The issue appears to be specific to the Kimi Code model integration. * File tool bridge appears to lose content between tool execution and filesystem write.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"709a85ea2a0805b8\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.82117355\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"49b08a4293e38576\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2026.3.7 regression: kimi-coding/k2p5 emits literal exec(. ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"49b08a4293e38576\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39907\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0667113ab9797367\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Bug]: 2026.3.7 regression: kimi-coding/k2p5 emits literal exec(...) text instead of structured tool calls #39907. [[Bug]: 2026.3.7 regression: kimi-coding/k2p5 emits literal exec(...) text instead of structured tool calls](#top)#39907. After upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7, `kimi-coding/k2p5` in the Control UI no longer reliably invokes tools. Instead of producing a real Exec tool event/card, it sometimes replies with plain assistant text claiming completion or literally prints `exec({...})` into the chat. 5. Observe that Kimi may output plain text such as `Done...` or literal `exec({\\\"command\\\": ...})` in the chat instead of producing a real `Exec` tool card/event. `kimi-coding/k2p5` should emit a structured tool call that OpenClaw executes, with the Control UI showing a real `Exec` tool card just like the working Gemini path. Kimi sometimes emits plain assistant text or literal fake tool-call text such as `exec({\\\"command\\\":\\\"mkdir -p ~/Downloads/test_folder2\\\"})` into the chat. Affected: users relying on `kimi-coding/k2p5` for real tool execution in Control UI sessions. * `google/gemini-3-flash-preview`: produces a real `Exec` tool card and actually runs the command on the same machine.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0667113ab9797367\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.81595254\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7604b8a433fb091d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Regression Bug]: OpenClaw browser profile ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7604b8a433fb091d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/30570\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"870968eba092f9d7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSummary. Browser control service starts but immediately disconnects in openclaw profile mode. Last known good version. 2026.2.22 or earlier\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"870968eba092f9d7\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.80070794\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"593651f3b3146b7e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: macOS app v2026.2.26 is arm64-only — regression ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"593651f3b3146b7e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/28877\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fa8e104e5b60d9f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe macOS app shipped in v2026.2.26 is arm64-only. It crashes immediately on Intel Macs with \\\"You can't open the application 'OpenClaw' because\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fa8e104e5b60d9f\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.79901963\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cd5d908b7cc6d166\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: You made openclaw a broken disaster, nothing works\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cd5d908b7cc6d166\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/35077\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a172ced0484b8640\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBug type. Regression (worked before, now fails). Summary. After doing an ubuntu vm complete reinstall to version 2026.3.2, nothing works.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a172ced0484b8640\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.7940821\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues \"openclaw/openclaw/issues\" regression OR bug OR docs \"2026\"","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":1827,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"39b17a9dce303e8f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: OpenClaw 2026.3.8 regression: empty agent ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"39b17a9dce303e8f\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0e5029a6115314dc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Reload](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270) to refresh your session.You signed out in another tab or window. *   [Sponsor](https://github.com/sponsors/openclaw). *   [Code](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw). *   [Issues 5k+](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues). *   [Pull requests 5k+](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pulls). *   [Security 368](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security). *   [Code](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw). *   [Issues](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues). *   [