ssues/41462#event-23411096977). [on Mar 9, 2026](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41462#event-23411099818). [#32991](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/32991). *   [Fix tool dispatch for malformed or missing tool call names #43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312). Root Cause 2 (Session Corruption) – PR [#41745](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/41745). Root Cause 1 (Tool Dispatching Regression) – PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) / Issue [#43283](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/43283). PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (lynnzc) identified the specific mechanism: OpenAI-compatible providers like Kimi emit malformed tool call names (functions:read, functions:exec) instead of canonical names (read, exec). Issue [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) – Independent confirmation of the same regression. Our issue is listed as a high-severity open regression alongside [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) and [#42270](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270), confirming that the tool dispatch failure is one of the most actively tracked blockers in the community right now. PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (tool-name normalization for Kimi's functions:exec format) was closed without merge due to reviewer concerns about the fuzzy endsWith inference logic. this looks related to [#41462](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41462) — the symptom is identical: all tools returning \\\"Tool not found\\\" immediately after upgrading from 2026.3.1 to 2026.3.2, with 2026.3.1 working fine.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb3fb6cb89209d0a\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99987566\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"90196216d3590034\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSubagents return empty output (0 tokens) after upgrade to ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_