s://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (lynnzc) identified the specific mechanism: OpenAI-compatible providers like Kimi emit malformed tool call names (functions:read, functions:exec) instead of canonical names (read, exec). Issue [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) – Independent confirmation of the same regression. Our issue is listed as a high-severity open regression alongside [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) and [#42270](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270), confirming that the tool dispatch failure is one of the most actively tracked blockers in the community right now. PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (tool-name normalization for Kimi's functions:exec format) was closed without merge due to reviewer concerns about the fuzzy endsWith inference logic. this looks related to [#41462](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41462) — the symptom is identical: all tools returning \"Tool not found\" immediately after upgrading from 2026.3.1 to 2026.3.2, with 2026.3.1 working fine.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cb3fb6cb89209d0a\">>>","score":0.99987566},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"90196216d3590034\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSubagents return empty output (0 tokens) after upgrade to ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"90196216d3590034\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/47315","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"144d55cbdf4cb3c5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExecutive Summary. On 2026-03-17, OpenClaw 3.13 introduced a Cliproxy OAuth regression that broke Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.6 with HTTP 400 errors.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"144d55cbdf4cb3c5\">>>","score":0.9998697},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"732c210fd1c52b0d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Local Chief ignores MEMORY.md and treats my own ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"732c210fd1c52b0d\">>>","u