nctions:read, functions:exec) instead of canonical names (read, exec). Issue [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) – Independent confirmation of the same regression. Our issue is listed as a high-severity open regression alongside [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) and [#42270](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270), confirming that the tool dispatch failure is one of the most actively tracked blockers in the community right now. PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (tool-name normalization for Kimi's functions:exec format) was closed without merge due to reviewer concerns about the fuzzy endsWith inference logic. this looks related to [#41462](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41462) — the symptom is identical: all tools returning \"Tool not found\" immediately after upgrading from 2026.3.1 to 2026.3.2, with 2026.3.1 working fine.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"313b353849a06bab\">>>","score":0.99863297},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f3d86f54318b21a2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: The OpenClaw Gateway fails to start after installation.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f3d86f54318b21a2\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/27316","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"85303427e158c6a1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... The OpenClaw Gateway fails to start after installation. [[Bug]: The OpenClaw Gateway fails to start after installation.](#top)#27316. # [Bug]: The OpenClaw Gateway fails to start after installation. · Existing OpenClaw installation detected, upgrading. · Active Node.js: v22.22.0 (/usr/bin/node). · Installing OpenClaw v2026.2.25. ✗ Restarting gateway service failed — re-run with --verbose for details. Restarted systemd service: openclaw-gateway.service. Timed out after 60s waiting for gateway port 18789 to become healthy. Gateway restart t